Q266 380 251 392T217 404Q177 404 142 372T93 290Q91 281 88 280T72 278H58Q52 284 52 289Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMATHI-3C0\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMATHI-78\" x=\"573\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> is irrational.</p>\n<p>This can be further simplified as follows:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"4.645ex\" height=\"0.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.171ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -73.8 2000 147.5\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-5-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-5-Title\">\\qquad</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\"></defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></g>\n</svg></span> The product of any rational number and <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.332ex\" height=\"1.676ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -576.1 573.5 721.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-6-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-6-Title\">\\pi</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E6-MJMATHI-3C0\" d=\"M132 -11Q98 -11 98 22V33L111 61Q186 219 220 334L228 358H196Q158 358 142 355T103 336Q92 329 81 318T62 297T53 285Q51 284 38 284Q19 284 19 294Q19 300 38 329T93 391T164 429Q171 431 389 431Q549 431 553 430Q573 423 573 402Q573 371 541 360Q535 358 472 358H408L405 341Q393 269 393 222Q393 170 402 129T421 65T431 37Q431 20 417 5T381 -10Q370 -10 363 -7T347 17T331 77Q330 86 330 121Q330 170 339 226T357 318T367 358H269L268 354Q268 351 249 275T206 114T175 17Q164 -11 132 -11Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E6-MJMATHI-3C0\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> is irrational.</p>\n<p>Therefore, the answer is \"II only.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> This statement is false since zero is rational and <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"4.174ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1796.9 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-7-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-7-Title\">\\pi\\cdot 0</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E7-MJMATHI-3C0\" d=\"M132 -11Q98 -11 98 22V33L111 61Q186 219 220 334L228 358H196Q158 358 142 355T103 336Q92 329 81 318T62 297T53 285Q51 284 38 284Q19 284 19 294Q19 300 38 329T93 391T164 429Q171 431 389 431Q549 431 553 430Q573 423 573 402Q573 371 541 360Q535 358 472 358H408L405 341Q393 269 393 222Q393 170 402 129T421 65T431 37Q431 20 417 5T381 -10Q370 -10 363 -7T347 17T331 77Q330 86 330 121Q330 170 339 226T357 318T367 358H269L268 354Q268 351 249 275T206 114T175 17Q164 -11 132 -11Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E7-MJMAIN-22C5\" d=\"M78 250Q78 274 95 292T138 310Q162 310 180 294T199 251Q199 226 182 208T139 190T96 207T78 250Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E7-MJMAIN-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E7-MJMATHI-3C0\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E7-MJMAIN-22C5\" x=\"795\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E7-MJMAIN-3